<title>JAPAN: Kyushu Oil to up reformer capacity to 27,000 bpd.</title>
<headline>Kyushu Oil to up reformer capacity to 27,000 bpd.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kyushu Oil Co Ltd said on Friday it will raise the capacity of its catalytic reformer at Oita refinery in western Japan to 27,000 barrels-per-day (bpd) from the current 21,000 bpd in November.</p>
<p>Kyushu Oil plans to expand the reformer capacity to boost the output of xylene, which will be used as feedstock at a new paraxylene plant due to start commercial operations at the refinery next April, a company official said.</p>
<p>The paraxylene plant, with an annual production capacity of 300,000 tonnes, is a joint venture between Kyushu Oil and Mitsubishi Oil Co Ltd. Paraxylene is mainly used to produce polyester fibre.</p>
</text>
